# The suites of tools/suite.list on Windows (Git Bash of the GitHub runner, Maat 1.6.0): one CI job per group
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml, job windows-gruppo), `tools/suite.sh --gruppi tools/suite-gruppi-windows.list --gruppo k/n`.
# Lines: «<group> [VAR=value …] <entry>» (the entry runs in that group, with those variables) and «- <entry> <reason>»
# (left out on Windows: counted as covered, written as ESCLUSA in riepilogo.txt). Every entry of suite.list in exactly
# one line; groups 1..n (tools/suite.sh refuses otherwise, tools/suite.test.sh checks the link with ci.yml).
# Groups 1, 2 and 3 are the subset that runs at every push (WIN_BREVE in ci.yml): 1 and 2 are exactly the entries of
# tools/prova-breve-windows.list (the short proof), 3 the expected outputs of the public corpus (the proof of the
# decider on Windows). The others run on pull requests to main, tags, main, workflow_dispatch, and pushes whose commit
# message says [windows completo]. Times: docs/piani notes of block D (CI) until block E rebalances them.

# left out on Windows
- test-fast            needs rsync and flock: on Windows it runs in WSL, which the runner does not have (locally at release)
- counterproof         needs rsync and flock: on Windows it runs in WSL, which the runner does not have (locally at release)
- vitest-classify      needs rsync and flock: on Windows it runs in WSL, which the runner does not have (locally at release)
- comandi-equivalenza  needs rsync and flock: on Windows it runs in WSL, which the runner does not have (locally at release)
- tools/oracolo.test.sh  about 70 minutes in Git Bash; logic that does not depend on the platform: it runs on Linux and macOS
- rollback             leaves in 1.6.0 (D4: no bash engine to go back to); ROLLBACK_TEST_RAPIDO alone took about 52 minutes in Git Bash

# group 1: the short proof, first half
1 tools/suite.test.sh
1 gates
1 test-review-surface
1 bash-node
1 stop-hook
1 blocks-independent
1 phase-usage
1 session-start

# group 2: the short proof, second half
2 guard
2 cycle-report
2 messages
2 maat-paths
2 senza-wsl
2 genericita
2 context-pack
2 maat-config
2 phase-events
2 harness-merge

# group 3: the expected outputs of the public corpus
3 tools/esempi-equiv.test.sh

# groups 4-7: the long suites, and the rest
4 DRIVER_TEST_RAPIDO=1 driver
5 cycle-state
6 run-phase
7 plan-check
7 finalize
7 ciclo-worktree
7 maat-doctor
7 spazi
